**Read:** [Tratamento de Minérios — CETEM, sixth edition](../sources/Tratamento-de-Minerios-CETEM.lingua#r_04ZQFADZ3NC3T6QDPQ565W1ERA), the complete screening and classification chapters; [Tratamento de Minérios: Práticas Laboratoriais — Sampaio, França, and Braga](../sources/CETEM-Praticas-Laboratoriais.lingua#r_44AAWXB1D7MBR9B0V3TYB8GF9B), the full applicable screening/classification procedures; [Introduction to Mineral Processing — Arun Kumar Majumder, NPTEL](../sources/Introduction-to-Mineral-Processing-NPTEL.lingua#r_5VQ67PA1160RQ1EWN17211XBWD), the complete industrial-screening and classification lecture material.

Screening and fluid classification divide a particle population using different physical mechanisms. Aperture or a nominal cut size does not specify the entire split. Size/shape/density, moisture/slurry, loading, orientation, residence, equipment condition, and method influence the result.

A partition curve relates a defined feed population to a product under a stated basis and size method. Bypass, misplacement, sharpness, short-circuiting, and changing feed can affect interpretation. A corrected curve and an observed partition answer different questions; preserve the transformation and assumptions.

Close total and size-fraction balances with compatible sampling/time supports. Product size distributions and mass yields together constrain the split; neither alone is enough to recover every feed component. Small or biased samples can produce implausible curves despite a smooth fitted model.

**Work:** complete a full screening/classification test and independently reconstruct a partition curve from feed/product data. Check fraction and total closure, quantify a stated misplacement/sharpness measure, and compare a plausible sampling/bypass explanation. Identify an independent test under changed feed or duty.

Read full chapter and lab methods. The next hydrocyclone and concentration studies retain the difference between observed population splits, corrected descriptions, equipment models, and process outcomes.

